		<div class="entry">
			<div class="post" id="post-166">
				<h2><a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/2010/07/10/joining-the-renovation-nation-in-roanokes-historic-district/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Joining Renovation Nation in Roanoke&#8217;s Historic District">Joining Renovation Nation in Roanoke&#8217;s Historic District</a></h2>
<div class="allinfos"><span class="date">July 10th, 2010</span>&nbsp; | &nbsp;<span class="category">Posted in <a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/category/real-estate/" title="View all posts in Real Estate" rel="category tag">Real Estate</a></span> by Mike Dame&nbsp; | &nbsp;<span class="comments"><a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/2010/07/10/joining-the-renovation-nation-in-roanokes-historic-district/#comments" title="Comment on Joining Renovation Nation in Roanoke&#8217;s Historic District">2 Comments</a> </span></div>

					<p>We&#8217;re very proud of Valeria&#8217;s renovation of a circa 1905 American Four Square home in the up-and-coming Mountain View Neighborhood in downtown Roanoke. The restoration project team partnered with the city&#8217;s Architectural Review Board to maintain the integrity of the original structure while adding modern conveniences.</p>
                                        <p><a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/2010/07/10/joining-the-renovation-nation-in-roanokes-historic-district/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Joining Renovation Nation in Roanoke&#8217;s Historic District"><strong>READ THIS POST ></strong></a></P>

 </div></div>
		<div class="entry">
			<div class="post" id="post-153">
				<h2><a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/2010/03/03/reaching-a-community-of-one/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Reaching a &#8216;Community of One&#8217;">Reaching a &#8216;Community of One&#8217;</a></h2>
<div class="allinfos"><span class="date">March 3rd, 2010</span>&nbsp; | &nbsp;<span class="category">Posted in <a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/category/marketing/" title="View all posts in Marketing" rel="category tag">Marketing</a>, <a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/category/social-media/" title="View all posts in Social Media" rel="category tag">Social Media</a></span> by Mike Dame&nbsp; | &nbsp;<span class="comments"><a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/2010/03/03/reaching-a-community-of-one/#respond" title="Comment on Reaching a &#8216;Community of One&#8217;">No Comments</a> </span></div>

					<p>In this age of oft-times impersonal, shotgun-style marketing, it&#8217;s easy to lose sight of the larger goal of making personal connections, one consumer at a time. That will be the topic of my presentation next month in Atlanta at the National Forum on Customer Based Marketing Strategies. I&#8217;ll be presenting a case study of my [...]</p>
                                        <p><a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/2010/03/03/reaching-a-community-of-one/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Reaching a &#8216;Community of One&#8217;"><strong>READ THIS POST ></strong></a></P>

 </div></div>
		<div class="entry">
			<div class="post" id="post-143">
				<h2><a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/2009/09/08/dameco-inc-launches-site-for-home-accessibilities/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to DameCo Inc. launches site for Home Accessibilities">DameCo Inc. launches site for Home Accessibilities</a></h2>
<div class="allinfos"><span class="date">September 8th, 2009</span>&nbsp; | &nbsp;<span class="category">Posted in <a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/category/green-building/" title="View all posts in Green Building" rel="category tag">Green Building</a></span> by Mike Dame&nbsp; | &nbsp;<span class="comments"><a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/2009/09/08/dameco-inc-launches-site-for-home-accessibilities/#comments" title="Comment on DameCo Inc. launches site for Home Accessibilities">2 Comments</a> </span></div>

					<p>This is a bit of a belated announcement, but in late July we launched the Web site for Home Accessibilities, a new residential design firm based in Winter Park, Florida, near Orlando. Home Accessibilities is the brainchild of Karen Kassik, a good friend who has been designing custom homes and remodeling existing homes for over 20 [...]</p>
                                        <p><a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/2009/09/08/dameco-inc-launches-site-for-home-accessibilities/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to DameCo Inc. launches site for Home Accessibilities"><strong>READ THIS POST ></strong></a></P>

 </div></div>
		<div class="entry">
			<div class="post" id="post-139">
				<h2><a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/2009/08/07/welcoming-our-cnr2030-advisory-board/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Welcoming our CNR2030 Advisory Board">Welcoming our CNR2030 Advisory Board</a></h2>
<div class="allinfos"><span class="date">August 7th, 2009</span>&nbsp; | &nbsp;<span class="category">Posted in <a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/category/cnr-2030/" title="View all posts in CNR 2030" rel="category tag">CNR 2030</a>, <a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/category/roanoke-cclp/" title="View all posts in Roanoke CCLP" rel="category tag">Roanoke CCLP</a></span> by admin&nbsp; | &nbsp;<span class="comments"><a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/2009/08/07/welcoming-our-cnr2030-advisory-board/#comments" title="Comment on Welcoming our CNR2030 Advisory Board">10 Comments</a> </span></div>

					<p>Our CNR2030 Advisory Board is gathering next Thursday for its first meeting, and we&#8217;ll be sharing news with them regarding Lumenhaus, Virginia Tech&#8217;s 2009 entry to the U.S. Department of Energy Solar Decathlon competition.</p>
                                        <p><a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/2009/08/07/welcoming-our-cnr2030-advisory-board/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Welcoming our CNR2030 Advisory Board"><strong>READ THIS POST ></strong></a></P>

 </div></div>
		<div class="entry">
			<div class="post" id="post-117">
				<h2><a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/2009/07/06/my-afternoon-with-air-mcnair/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to My afternoon with Air McNair">My afternoon with Air McNair</a></h2>
<div class="allinfos"><span class="date">July 6th, 2009</span>&nbsp; | &nbsp;<span class="category">Posted in <a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/category/miscellaneous/" title="View all posts in Miscellaneous" rel="category tag">Miscellaneous</a></span> by Mike Dame&nbsp; | &nbsp;<span class="comments"><a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/2009/07/06/my-afternoon-with-air-mcnair/#comments" title="Comment on My afternoon with Air McNair">7 Comments</a> </span></div>

					<p>In 1994, while on the road covering the Florida Gators&#8217; game at Ole Miss, I took a side trip down the Natchez Trace to report on the biggest story in southern football that season: Alcorn State quarterback Steve &#8220;Air&#8221; McNair.</p>
                                        <p><a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/2009/07/06/my-afternoon-with-air-mcnair/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to My afternoon with Air McNair"><strong>READ THIS POST ></strong></a></P>

Tags: <a href="http://www.damecoinc.com/tag/steve-mcnair/" rel="tag">Steve McNair</a>  </div></div>
		
